* MiCA Titles III–IV\nStablecoins
** Two categories
*** EMT: one official currency, deemed e-money
*** ART: any other value or basket
*** Only the issuer may offer (or consent)
*** Applied since 30 June 2024
** ART authorisation (Arts 16–26)
*** EU legal person authorised, or credit institution (Art. 17)
*** Exempt below EUR 5 000 000 or qualified investors
*** Application: legal opinion, governance, plans
*** 25 + 60 + 20 + 25 working days
*** ECB veto on payment systems, monetary policy
*** White paper approved with the authorisation
** Reporting and use limits
*** Quarterly report above EUR 100 000 000 (Art. 22)
*** Stop issuing above 1 million tx and EUR 200 million per day (Art. 23)
** Issuer obligations (Arts 27–35)
*** Conduct, marketing, monthly disclosure
*** Governance, complaints, conflicts
*** Own funds: max(EUR 350 000, 2 % reserve, 1/4 overheads)
*** Add-ons up to 20 % (40 % in stress)
** Reserve (Arts 36–40)
*** Legally and operationally segregated
*** ≥ 30 % bank deposits per currency
*** Custody at CASP, bank or investment firm
*** Investment in highly liquid low-risk instruments
*** Six-monthly independent audit
*** Permanent redemption at market value, no fee
*** No interest (Art. 40)
** Significant ART (Arts 43–45)
*** 3 of 7 criteria: 10 M holders, EUR 5 bn, 2.5 M tx/day...
*** EBA supervision
*** Own funds 3 %, deposits ≥ 60 %
*** Liquidity stress tests, open custody
** Recovery and redemption plans (Arts 46–47)
*** Liquidity fees, redemption limits, suspension
*** Orderly redemption with temporary administrator
** E-money tokens (Arts 48–58)
*** Credit institution or e-money institution only
*** Notify 40 working days; white paper 20 working days
*** Issued and redeemed at par, no fee
*** No interest (Art. 50)
*** ≥ 30 % deposits, rest in same-currency liquid assets
*** Significant EMT: ART reserve regime applies
*** 80 % home-concentration carve-out for non-euro EU currencies
